\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces Initial-condition hand-off (Sec.~\ref {subsec:ic_why_tk} explains why this reconstruction is necessary at all). From each \textsc  {CosmoGridV1} run's stored \textsc  {concept} perturbations, the CDM+baryon transfer function at $a=1$ is extracted as a two-column $(k,\,-T/k^2)$ table (\texttt  {pkdgrav/get\_transfer\_function.py}); the clustering amplitude \mbox  {$\sigma _{8,cb}$} is computed from that same CDM+baryon spectrum, so table and normalisation describe one field, and a matched \textsc  {class} solve with three massive neutrino states supplies the derived \mbox  {$\Omega _r$}; \texttt  {IC\_preparation.py} patches these into \texttt  {cosmology.par}; \textsc  {PkdGrav3} generates the backscaled particle load, which the \emph  {two solvers of this thesis} then consume byte-identically. Note that this load is deliberately \emph  {not} a reproduction of \textsc  {CosmoGridV1}'s own native initial conditions, which were generated through \textsc  {concept}'s forward linear evolution rather than by backscaling a static table; the resulting difference is quantified in Sec.~\ref {sec:shell_validation}.}}{17}{figure.2.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ic_flow}{{2.2}{17}{Initial-condition hand-off (Sec.~\ref {subsec:ic_why_tk} explains why this reconstruction is necessary at all). From each \textsc {CosmoGridV1} run's stored \textsc {concept} perturbations, the CDM+baryon transfer function at $a=1$ is extracted as a two-column $(k,\,-T/k^2)$ table (\texttt {pkdgrav/get\_transfer\_function.py}); the clustering amplitude \mbox {$\sigma _{8,cb}$} is computed from that same CDM+baryon spectrum, so table and normalisation describe one field, and a matched \textsc {class} solve with three massive neutrino states supplies the derived \mbox {$\Omega _r$}; \texttt {IC\_preparation.py} patches these into \texttt {cosmology.par}; \textsc {PkdGrav3} generates the backscaled particle load, which the \emph {two solvers of this thesis} then consume byte-identically. Note that this load is deliberately \emph {not} a reproduction of \textsc {CosmoGridV1}'s own native initial conditions, which were generated through \textsc {concept}'s forward linear evolution rather than by backscaling a static table; the resulting difference is quantified in Sec.~\ref {sec:shell_validation}}{figure.2.2}{}}
