\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.10}{\ignorespaces The diffusion pipeline (\texttt  {ml/diffusion/model.py}). Top: the EDM denoiser is the U-Net of Figure~\ref {fig:film_unet} wrapped in the four preconditioning coefficients of Eq.~\eqref  {eq:edm_coeffs}. Solid arrows carry data, dashed arrows carry conditioning. The input $x$ enters from above: it is variance-normalised by \mbox  {$c_{\mathrm  {in}}$} and concatenated with the (never-noised) low patch, while a skip path ($c_{\mathrm  {skip}}\,x$) feeds directly to the addition node. The noise level $\sigma $ enters from below, setting \mbox  {$c_{\mathrm  {in}}$} and \mbox  {$c_{\mathrm  {out}}$} via Eq.~\eqref  {eq:edm_coeffs}, and conditioning the U-Net through \mbox  {$c_{\mathrm  {noise}}$} via FiLM. The output blends the identity path with the network's contribution (\mbox  {$c_{\mathrm  {out}} F_\theta $}), shifting smoothly from ``pass through'' at low \mbox  {$\sigma $} to ``generate'' at high \mbox  {$\sigma $}. Bottom: sampling starts from pure noise and applies 32 Heun steps down the Karras schedule, producing a sample that targets the high-pass residual $\delta _{\mathrm  {high}} - \delta _{\mathrm  {low}}$; composing it back onto the low map, $\delta _{\mathrm  {low}} + \mathrm  {HP}(\delta _{\mathrm  {high}} - \delta _{\mathrm  {low}})$, is what keeps the large scales \textsc  {Disco-DJ}'s exactly.}}{30}{figure.2.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:edm_sampling}{{2.10}{30}{The diffusion pipeline (\texttt {ml/diffusion/model.py}). Top: the EDM denoiser is the U-Net of Figure~\ref {fig:film_unet} wrapped in the four preconditioning coefficients of Eq.~\eqref {eq:edm_coeffs}. Solid arrows carry data, dashed arrows carry conditioning. The input $x$ enters from above: it is variance-normalised by \mbox {$c_{\mathrm {in}}$} and concatenated with the (never-noised) low patch, while a skip path ($c_{\mathrm {skip}}\,x$) feeds directly to the addition node. The noise level $\sigma $ enters from below, setting \mbox {$c_{\mathrm {in}}$} and \mbox {$c_{\mathrm {out}}$} via Eq.~\eqref {eq:edm_coeffs}, and conditioning the U-Net through \mbox {$c_{\mathrm {noise}}$} via FiLM. The output blends the identity path with the network's contribution (\mbox {$c_{\mathrm {out}} F_\theta $}), shifting smoothly from ``pass through'' at low \mbox {$\sigma $} to ``generate'' at high \mbox {$\sigma $}. Bottom: sampling starts from pure noise and applies 32 Heun steps down the Karras schedule, producing a sample that targets the high-pass residual $\delta _{\mathrm {high}} - \delta _{\mathrm {low}}$; composing it back onto the low map, $\delta _{\mathrm {low}} + \mathrm {HP}(\delta _{\mathrm {high}} - \delta _{\mathrm {low}})$, is what keeps the large scales \textsc {Disco-DJ}'s exactly}{figure.2.10}{}}
