\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Getting \textsc  {Disco-DJ} onto \textsc  {PkdGrav3}, one fix at a time (\texttt  {vis/plot\_ic\_error\_budget.py}). Each curve is a $z=0$ matter power spectrum divided by the \textsc  {PkdGrav3} run started from the same initial conditions; percentages are medians over $k \in [0.01, 0.02]\,h/$Mpc, the largest scales the $900\,\mathrm  {Mpc}/h$ box represents. All four are simulations performed during setup validation, so this is the actual debugging history rather than an illustration of it. \new  {The reference in each ratio is the \textsc  {PkdGrav3} run started from the same initial conditions as that stage, so that the quantity compared is always ``\textsc  {Disco-DJ} against the reference started from the same ICs''. Stages~(2) and~(3) share the same reference run; stages~(1) and~(4) each use their own, and the references are therefore not interchangeable between stages.} \textcolor {orange}{JB: is it so? Isn't the reference=cosmogrid sim the same in all four lines?} The steep common decline beyond $k \approx 0.2\,h/$Mpc is \textsc  {Disco-DJ}'s particle-mesh force resolution in these deliberately cheap validation runs, not an initial-condition effect; the deficit the correction pipelines actually face is measured on the production lightcones in Sec.~\ref {sec:shell_validation}.}}{34}{figure.3.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ic_error_budget}{{3.1}{34}{Getting \textsc {Disco-DJ} onto \textsc {PkdGrav3}, one fix at a time (\texttt {vis/plot\_ic\_error\_budget.py}). Each curve is a $z=0$ matter power spectrum divided by the \textsc {PkdGrav3} run started from the same initial conditions; percentages are medians over $k \in [0.01, 0.02]\,h/$Mpc, the largest scales the $900\,\mathrm {Mpc}/h$ box represents. All four are simulations performed during setup validation, so this is the actual debugging history rather than an illustration of it. \new {The reference in each ratio is the \textsc {PkdGrav3} run started from the same initial conditions as that stage, so that the quantity compared is always ``\textsc {Disco-DJ} against the reference started from the same ICs''. Stages~(2) and~(3) share the same reference run; stages~(1) and~(4) each use their own, and the references are therefore not interchangeable between stages.} \jozef {is it so? Isn't the reference=cosmogrid sim the same in all four lines?} The steep common decline beyond $k \approx 0.2\,h/$Mpc is \textsc {Disco-DJ}'s particle-mesh force resolution in these deliberately cheap validation runs, not an initial-condition effect; the deficit the correction pipelines actually face is measured on the production lightcones in Sec.~\ref {sec:shell_validation}}{figure.3.1}{}}
